    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a public company traded under the ticker LUMN, headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana, with CIK 0000018926. On its own site the company describes itself as a provider of secure networking, edge cloud and AI-ready infrastructure built on a global fiber network, and calls itself the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy. It says its fiber footprint reaches across markets and is intended to reduce latency for real-time performance.\n\nThe site presents the network as programmable and consumption-based, with diverse 100G paths and automatic failover. Customer material describes work for the New York Yankees, moving data and media between Yankee Stadium and digital operations facilities in Tampa, and for American Family Care, an urgent care provider scaling across 26 states that the company says needed a private, low-latency network for heavy AI workloads. It also cites Arctic Glacier, where built-in automation replaced manual operations, and Prometheus Hyperscale, which anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady. Retail use cases cited include real-time inventory, AI-driven personalization, transaction security and DDoS protection.\n\nBeyond the site material, the company's record shows no individual lawsuits and no tracked products or MCP servers. Its litigation exposure is counted at 57 in Louisiana.",
